<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
  <p class="font-bold">
    Two identical capacitors share charge, but only half the initial energy remains stored.
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-base">
    <div class="border-2 border-ink p-3">
      <strong>Before connecting</strong>
      <p>Capacitor 1: voltage V</p>
      <p>Capacitor 2: empty</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-bold">Stored energy = ½CV²</p>
    </div>
    <div class="border-2 border-ink p-3">
      <strong>After settling</strong>
      <p>Each capacitor: voltage V/2</p>
      <p>Each holds half the charge</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-bold">Total energy = ¼CV²</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 300 122"
    class="w-full max-w-sm"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="capacitor-title capacitor-desc"
  >
    <title id="capacitor-title">Half the initial stored energy transfers outside the capacitors</title>
    <desc id="capacitor-desc">
      Of the initial energy, one half remains in the two capacitors and one half transfers via
      the connecting circuit and fields.
    </desc>
    <rect x="10" y="32" width="280" height="30" fill="#d7a13d" />
    <rect x="10" y="32" width="140" height="30" fill="#387a91" />
    <rect x="10" y="74" width="14" height="14" fill="#387a91" />
    <rect x="10" y="98" width="14" height="14" fill="#d7a13d" />
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="16">
      <text x="10" y="22">
        Initial energy
      </text>
      <text x="32" y="87">
        ½ remains stored
      </text>
      <text x="32" y="111">
        ½ leaves the capacitors
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">
    Each final capacitor stores ½C(V/2)², so together they store ¼CV²: half the original ½CV².
    The other half is transferred to heating, electromagnetic fields or radiation during the
    current flow. An ideal resistance-free circuit cannot simply be assumed to settle instantly
    into that static state.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
